{% comment %}
  F1GENZ Reviews + Q&A - copy-paste snippets for a Sapo .bwt theme.
  Replace API_HOST with the app API URL (https://...) and STORE_DOMAIN with the store's x.mysapo.net domain.
  The app stores the same pair in the shop metafield f1genz.config (JSON string) and as plain strings in
  f1genz.api_url and f1genz.store_domain. No snippet here reads them: paste the two values literally.
  The runtime fetches ratings, reviews and Q&A from the API. Only block 4b prints metafields: the two scalar
  product metafields f1genz_reviews.rating_avg and f1genz_reviews.rating_count, guarded by an if tag.
  Filters used: escape only. Include tags only, never slice.
  For the SEO JSON-LD use storefront/theme/f1genz-product-schema.bwt instead of anything here.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %} 1. Global loader - layout file, before </body> {% endcomment %}
<script>
  window.__F1GENZ_STOREFRONT_CONFIG = {
    apiUrl: "https://API_HOST",
    storeDomain: "STORE_DOMAIN"
  };
</script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://API_HOST/storefront/f1genz-storefront.css">
<script src="https://API_HOST/storefront/f1genz-storefront.js" defer></script>

{% comment %} 2. Reviews + Q&A widget - product.bwt. customer-email and customer-phone are the only source of shopper identity; empty values mean a guest. {% endcomment %}
<div class="f1genz-sapo-review-section">
  <f1genz-reviews
    product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    storeDomain="STORE_DOMAIN"
    customer-email="{{ customer.email | escape }}"
    customer-phone="{{ customer.phone | escape }}"
  ></f1genz-reviews>
</div>

{% comment %} 3. Separate Q&A panel (use instead of 2 when reviews and Q&A sit in different places) {% endcomment %}
<div class="f1genz-sapo-review-section">
  <f1genz-qna-panel
    product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    storeDomain="STORE_DOMAIN"
    customer-email="{{ customer.email | escape }}"
    customer-phone="{{ customer.phone | escape }}"
  ></f1genz-qna-panel>
</div>

{% comment %} 4. Rating badge - product card / collection loop. Score is fetched in batches from the API. {% endcomment %}
<f1genz-rating-badge
  product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  storeDomain="STORE_DOMAIN"
></f1genz-rating-badge>

{% comment %}
  4b. Optional server-rendered badge, use INSTEAD of 4 (not in addition). Prints the two scalar metafields the app
  writes (f1genz_reviews.rating_avg string, f1genz_reviews.rating_count integer) behind an if tag guard;
  renders nothing while the metafield is missing.
{% endcomment %}
{% if product.metafields.f1genz_reviews.rating_count %}
<f1genz-rating-badge
  product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  storeDomain="STORE_DOMAIN"
  avg-rating="{{ product.metafields.f1genz_reviews.rating_avg }}"
  review-count="{{ product.metafields.f1genz_reviews.rating_count }}"
></f1genz-rating-badge>
{% endif %}

{% comment %} 5. Curated review slider (optional) - product.bwt, below the reviews widget. Needs product-id. The merchant switches it on or off and sets 5-15 cards under Settings > Display; the server enforces both and count is only a hint. {% endcomment %}
<f1genz-curated-slider
  product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  storeDomain="STORE_DOMAIN"
  count="6"
></f1genz-curated-slider>
